  "live_records": {
    "q-143828": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143828",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given in the table below. Find $\\text{E}[2XY].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.4$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables with supports ${S}_{X}$ and ${S}_{Y},$ respectively, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability mass function with support $S={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}.$ If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=2xy.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2)\\cdot f(1,2)+(2\\cdot 1\\cdot 4)\\cdot f(1,4)\\,+(2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2)\\cdot f(2,2)+(2\\cdot 2\\cdot 4)\\cdot f(2,4) \\\\  & =4\\cdot f(1,2)+8\\cdot f(1,4)+8\\cdot f(2,2)+16\\cdot f(2,4) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 0.1+8\\cdot 0.25+8\\cdot 0.25+16\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =0.4+2+2+6.4 \\\\  & =10.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
