    "q-111898": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111898",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Find $\\text{E}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(X+Y)],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}},\\, & 0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le x, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y).\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le x\\},$ where $f(x)$ is nonzero.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14154787/assets/a4f7e4e3f5e6a46fdc1b61a40986aec7b47fe75b37c8f042497aa0f3a0969f30.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(X+Y)] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)]}_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
